-- 027: school price board ("whiteboard"). One row per school with the school's OWN published cost of attendance,
-- its year, basis (on-campus etc.) and the page it came from. The app shows these in place of the federal estimate,
-- and falls back to the estimate for schools with no row. NOT RUN. Take a manual Supabase export first.
-- Updating prices later needs NO deploy: change rows here (Supabase table editor, or ask Claude). Readers: everyone.
-- Writers: nobody through the app (no insert/update/delete policy), only the project owner / service role.
create table if not exists public.school_costs (
  school_id     text primary key,
  academic_year text not null check (academic_year ~ '^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}$'),
  basis         text check (basis in ('on-campus','off-campus','commuter','not-stated')),
  in_state      jsonb,
  out_of_state  jsonb,
  source_url    text not null check (source_url ~ '^https://'),
  checked       date,
  confidence    text check (confidence in ('high','medium','low')),
  notes         text,
  updated_at    timestamptz not null default now()
);
alter table public.school_costs enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "read school costs" on public.school_costs;
create policy "read school costs" on public.school_costs for select to anon, authenticated using (true);

insert into public.school_costs (school_id, academic_year, basis, in_state, out_of_state, source_url, checked, confidence, notes) values
  ('sc-129020','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 44230, "tuition": 17010, "fees": 4564, "housing": 10186, "food": 6896, "books": 1020, "transportation": 2494, "personal": 1968}'::jsonb,'{"total": 67108, "tuition": 39678, "fees": 4564, "housing": 10186, "food": 6896, "books": 1020, "transportation": 2704, "personal": 1968}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.uconn.edu/cost/','2026-10-14','high','Full-time Storrs undergraduate financial-aid COA estimates, distinct from the page''s initial direct-cost-only table. Both totals additionally include printed loan fees of $92; all printed components reconcile exactly. The published 2026-27 housing estimate explicitly uses average 2025-26 Storrs housing costs; this is the school''s current-year COA figure, not a substituted prior-year budget. Food uses the Value Meal Plan. The separate billing table uses $8,288 standard-double housing and separately lists waivable health insurance and the Husky Book Bundle; those figures were not added to COA. Printed off-campus totals: resident $45,674; nonresident $68,552. For Storrs students living with parents, housing $2,132, food $2,122 and personal $1,288 are printed without a separate total. New England Regional on-campus tuition is $26,028 and COA $53,458. The page also publishes regional-campus budgets.'),
  ('sc-130943','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 39154, "tuition": 15740, "fees": 2550, "housing": 9286, "food": 7328, "books": 1250, "transportation": 1000, "personal": 1942}'::jsonb,'{"total": 65884, "tuition": 42470, "fees": 2550, "housing": 9286, "food": 7328, "books": 1250, "transportation": 1000, "personal": 1942}'::jsonb,'https://www.udel.edu/students/student-financial-services/coa/','2026-10-14','high','Newark main-campus budget, full-time enrollment of 12+ credits, fall and spring, standard housing and food. These are estimated educational budgets; actual housing/food selections and programs can differ. Both totals additionally include printed loan fees of $58; all printed components reconcile exactly. Printed off-campus totals: resident $37,214; nonresident $63,944. Commuter totals: resident $27,210; nonresident $53,940. Differential charges apply to Business, Engineering, Music, Honors and Nursing; base figures do not represent these higher-cost programs. For students admitted from fall 2025, annual differentials are Nursing $2,500, Business $3,000, Engineering $4,000, Honors $2,000 and Music $1,250. Separate fee rows list new-student orientation $260 and international-student service $380; neither is included in the selected $2,550 mandatory-fee figure. Continuing-student differential rates also appear.'),
  ('sc-139940','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 34549.51, "tuition": 9270, "fees": 1320, "housing": 11864, "food": 4466, "books": 2066, "transportation": 1037.13, "personal": 4394.38}'::jsonb,'{"total": 56179.51, "tuition": 30900, "fees": 1320, "housing": 11864, "food": 4466, "books": 2066, "transportation": 1037.13, "personal": 4394.38}'::jsonb,'https://sfs.gsu.edu/resources/coa/2026-2027-cost-of-attendance/','2026-10-14','high','Bachelor''s Degree, Georgia Resident and Non-Resident, on-campus columns; excludes Perimeter/associate and out-of-country rates. Published cents cannot be represented as exact integer dollars without rounding: resident total $34,549.51; nonresident total $56,179.51; transportation $1,037.13 and personal expenses $4,394.38 for both. These six fields are null solely because of the integer constraint. Both printed totals equal all printed line items including Direct Loan Fees $132.00, which have no dedicated schema field. Other printed totals: off-campus $37,259.08/$58,889.28 and with relative $28,691.72/$50,321.72 (resident/nonresident). COA is an estimate. The linked overview says budgets cover fall and spring at 12 credits per semester. Totals, transportation and personal were filled from the exact printed amounts in this note.'),
  ('sc-151351','2026-27','not-stated','{"total": 30574, "tuition": 12142, "fees": null, "housing": 14398, "food": null, "books": 1320, "transportation": 284, "personal": 2430}'::jsonb,'{"total": 62956, "tuition": 42702, "fees": null, "housing": 14398, "food": null, "books": 1320, "transportation": 2106, "personal": 2430}'::jsonb,'https://www.studentcentral.indiana.edu/cost-of-iu/index.html','2026-10-14','high','Full-time undergraduate, full 2026-27 academic year (fall and spring); tuition allows 40 credits across fall, spring and intersessions. The table does not explicitly label its housing basis or print alternative living-arrangement budgets. Tuition combines tuition and mandatory fees; housing combines housing and food; fees and food are null. Both totals equal printed components. Costs are estimates and vary by student choices, travel habits and academic program. Page still says finalized estimates will be available this summer. Used the explicitly dated 2026-27 undergraduate table; undated image alternative text elsewhere on the same page contains different figures.'),
  ('sc-153603','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 26264, "tuition": 9816, "fees": 1586, "housing": 11162, "food": null, "books": 800, "transportation": 450, "personal": 2450}'::jsonb,'{"total": 46762, "tuition": 29864, "fees": 1586, "housing": 11162, "food": null, "books": 800, "transportation": 900, "personal": 2450}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.iastate.edu/getting-started/cost/cost-of-attendance/undergraduate-students/','2026-10-14','high','Fall and spring, full-time 12+ credits, dependent student, ordinary undergraduate tuition. Scripted estimator totals were read in the real cloud browser after selecting each residency; both totals equal printed components. Housing combines housing and food; food is null. Housing uses median campus housing and Cardinal meal plan. Special course fees excluded; some majors and upperclass students have higher tuition. Estimated 2026-27 figures are subject to change. Other displayed scenarios: off-campus dependent housing/food $9,960; independent $12,294; dependent resident with parent $5,305. Independent personal $2,850 and resident on-campus transportation $950; dependent off-campus transportation $950 resident/$1,400 nonresident. International rates are separate.'),
  ('sc-155317','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 33725, "tuition": 11844, "fees": 1065, "housing": 14370, "food": null, "books": 778, "transportation": 2600, "personal": 2962}'::jsonb,'{"total": 53660, "tuition": 31779, "fees": 1065, "housing": 14370, "food": null, "books": 778, "transportation": 2600, "personal": 2962}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.ku.edu/estimated-cost-of-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Estimated academic-year costs based on 30 credits. Housing combines housing and meals; separate food not published. Both totals include a separately printed $106 loan fee, outside the requested component fields; all printed components including this fee sum exactly to each total. Additional course fees excluded. Off-campus totals: resident $32,475, nonresident $52,410; combined housing and meals $13,120, other components unchanged. Financial-aid COA source retained; separate admissions page https://admissions.ku.edu/costs prints differing nonresident tuition and other allowances.'),
  ('sc-163286','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 34268, "tuition": 11014, "fees": 1820, "housing": 10290, "food": 7180, "books": 1250, "transportation": 1514, "personal": 1200}'::jsonb,'{"total": 65520, "tuition": 42266, "fees": 1820, "housing": 10290, "food": 7180, "books": 1250, "transportation": 1514, "personal": 1200}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.umd.edu/resources-policies/cost-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Estimated annual costs; both component sums equal printed totals. Housing includes cable and phone; food is an average. Off-campus totals: resident $36,066, nonresident $67,318; with-parent totals: $22,752/$54,004. Business, engineering and computer-science majors with 60+ credits incur differential tuition: financial-aid FAQ prints $1,687 per full-time semester; qualifying students may receive an offsetting grant. International students requiring university-issued immigration documents may incur $125 per semester. All charges subject to change. COA source prints resident tuition $11,014; separate 2026-27 catalog https://www.academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/fees-expenses-financial-aid/tuition-fees/ prints $11,015 and annual differential tuition $3,375. COA amounts retained.'),
  ('syracuse-university','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 95676, "tuition": 69180, "fees": 1869, "housing": 20580, "food": null, "books": 1847, "transportation": 839, "personal": 1294}'::jsonb,'{"total": 95676, "tuition": 69180, "fees": 1869, "housing": 20580, "food": null, "books": 1847, "transportation": 839, "personal": 1294}'::jsonb,'https://www.syracuse.edu/admissions-aid/cost/undergraduate-costs/','2026-10-14','high','Same published price for both residency categories, before aid. Housing combines housing and food (average); separate food not published. Printed total includes $67 loan fees if applicable; components plus loan fee sum exactly to $95,676. Mandatory health insurance $2,868 is additional unless waived for adequate private coverage; printed insured total $98,544. Off-campus total $93,398 ($96,266 insured); with-parents total $83,979 ($86,847 insured). Residential technology service fee mandatory with a university housing contract. First two years normally require university housing, with local-family commuter exception. Program/course fees may vary; page states upcoming-year figures remain estimates until May trustee approval.'),
  ('umass-amherst','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 8272, "housing": 9772, "personal": 1000, "total": 39896, "transportation": 400, "tuition": 19212}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 8272, "housing": 9772, "personal": 1000, "total": 63983, "transportation": 400, "tuition": 43299}'::jsonb,'https://www.umass.edu/financialaid/undergraduate-costs','2026-10-14','high','Full-time table, ''2026-2027 Costs (9-Month)''. The page prints a single combined ''Tuition & Fees'' line ($19,212 in-state / $43,299 out-of-state); that combined figure is recorded under tuition and fees is null because the page does not print them separately. Columns are headed ''On/Off Campus'' — the same budget applies to both, recorded as on-campus. Page states figures are estimates only, not final until approved by the UMass Board of Trustees. A New England Regional (NERSP) column is also printed (total $57,046). The page also prints an ''Average Federal Loan Fees'' line of $40 inside its indirect-cost subtotal; the schema has no field for it.'),
  ('university-of-colorado-boulder','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 39992, "tuition": 15014, "fees": null, "housing": 20682, "food": null, "books": 1200, "transportation": 1314, "personal": 1782}'::jsonb,'{"total": 71784, "tuition": 46058, "fees": null, "housing": 20682, "food": null, "books": 1200, "transportation": 2062, "personal": 1782}'::jsonb,'https://www.colorado.edu/financialaid/cost/example-aid','2026-10-14','high','Published financial-aid budget for new full-time undergraduates, fall and spring, at the base tuition tier. Tuition includes combined tuition and fees; housing includes combined housing and food. Resident tuition assumes application for and authorization of the College Opportunity Fund. Program-specific tuition tiers differ. Excludes the one-time $232 new-student fee. Housing/food uses an average residence-hall room, 19 meals weekly and an additional food allowance; actual selections can cost less. Printed off-campus totals: resident $37,850; nonresident $69,642. Resident living-with-parents total: $30,990. Some nonresidents belonging to American Indian Tribes with historical Colorado ties may qualify for resident tuition. Both selected totals equal all printed budget components; no discrepancy.'),
  ('university-of-new-hampshire','2026-27','not-stated','{"books": 1000, "fees": 3868, "food": 5624, "housing": 9960, "personal": 3796, "total": 40920, "transportation": 300, "tuition": 16304}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1000, "fees": 3868, "food": 5624, "housing": 9960, "personal": 3796, "total": 62862, "transportation": 550, "tuition": 37996}'::jsonb,'https://www.unh.edu/financialaid/costs','2026-10-14','high','Table headed ''Durham Undergraduate Cost of Attendance 2026-2027''. The page does not state a housing basis (on-campus/off-campus/commuter) for this table, so basis is not-stated. ''Miscellaneous'' is recorded under personal. A $68 ''Loan Fee'' line is printed and is included in the page''s total; the schema has no field for it. A NE Regional column is also printed (total $53,298). Page footnote: costs are estimated and subject to change.'),
  ('university-of-vermont','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1320, "fees": 3058, "food": null, "housing": 14654, "personal": 2442, "total": 38762, "transportation": 234, "tuition": 16938}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1320, "fees": 3058, "food": null, "housing": 14654, "personal": 2443, "total": 68878, "transportation": 630, "tuition": 46655}'::jsonb,'https://www.uvm.edu/studentfinancialservices/costs-attending','2026-10-14','high','Tables headed ''On-Campus Vermont Resident Student'' and ''On-Campus Out-of-State Resident Student'' under ''Undergraduate Tuition and Fees, 2026-2027 Academic Year Costs'' (12-19 credit hours, two semesters), read on the start_url page (its cost tables sit in paged sections). Base columns used: Program Fee $0. Students in select colleges/schools (Nursing & Health Sciences, Grossman Business, Engineering & Mathematical Sciences) pay a $1,000 Program Fee; those columns total $39,762 in-state / $69,878 out-of-state. The page prints one combined ''Average Food and Housing'' line ($14,654); it is recorded under housing and food is null. fees is the printed Comprehensive Fee ($3,058); the page also prints a separate $30 Residential Engagement Council (REC) Fee, not folded into fees. ''Estimated Miscellaneous Personal Expenses'' is recorded under personal. The printed totals include an ''Estimated Loan Fees'' line ($86 in-state / $88 out-of-state); the schema has no field for it.')
on conflict (school_id) do update set academic_year=excluded.academic_year, basis=excluded.basis, in_state=excluded.in_state,
  out_of_state=excluded.out_of_state, source_url=excluded.source_url, checked=excluded.checked, confidence=excluded.confidence,
  notes=excluded.notes, updated_at=now();

-- Rollback: drop table public.school_costs;   (the app then shows the federal estimates again, nothing else changes)
